441 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(      ay 1 will explore the Technology Frontier, asking what is coming. The day will have expert sessions and discussions on emerging technologies, the launch of the CSITM Tech Report, a technology expo, Frontier Labs, product showcases and NSRCEL product launch. Apart from the sessions, the day will also feature different activities and challenges.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

442 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(D)/Pg 13 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

443 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(    ay 2, Technology Meets Sectors, asks what will change. The day will explore six sectors: AI Tech, FinTech, HealthTech, EdTech, AgriTech, and ClimateTech & Energy. There will be panel discussions, expert talks and roundtable discussions exploring the impact of technology across these sectors. A Hardware Foundry along with activities like the Tech Escape Room, Open Quiz Challenge, and Agent vs Analyst, will be the other attractions of the day.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

444 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(      ay 3, India @ the Frontier, asks what India should build. The day will discuss India's potential and the global market. There will be a Lawmakers Conclave, a small-format session where policymakers and the people building tech sit in the same room and talk directly. Key activities include the FutureTech Pitch, Tech Hunt, and the final round of the FutureTech Challenge. The symposium will conclude with the Great Technology Debate followed by the closing keynote and the release of the Bengaluru Declaration on Technology 2030.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

